{
  "about": [
    "what every app says when you change your own emotes: add, remove, rename, swap, block, unblock. one file for every app.",
    "words: the line, by id, in english. {name} is the emote's name, {slot} the slot the server filed it in. lowercase, no trailing period.",
    "an app says it in its own notice (a toast on the site and the extension, a status line on the desktop and the terminal client) and in its own language: the english is the contract, the other languages translate it.",
    "answers: what the server's answer to a request is told as. op is the request, status the http status (0 = no answer at all: offline, timed out, blocked),",
    "says the id of the line. an answer this table does not list is read as the op's failed id. a runner that meets an id, an op or a field it does not know must fail, never skip.",
    "a request that is not logged in says login; a name that is already held says dupe; remove of a slot that is already empty is a remove that worked."
  ],
